Z||000029||Big O||03-02-2000||12:15 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DXR_DAD:<BR><B> Stimpy,  Give-a-ways, Door prizes, Raffels,???   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> .  Fiero parts? TIRES, TIERS, AND MORE TIRES,  Can you say d-i-s-c-o-u-n-t!!!!! .  I can't wait!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Somebody throw some water on him, I think he's going up in smoke.  DXer Dad, I got the flyers in the mail today and they are on their way around the neighborhood.  We will be sharing the show lot with the Modesto Throttlers, the biggest street rod club in the Central Valley.  They will be selling raffle tickets to raise money for charity.  They will be raffling off a souped up small block Chevy.  If you can bring some Fiero stuff to give out to the Fiero crowd as door prizes I think that would be great!  Sorry it's taken me so long to get in on the chat but I had a hard time finding the address of the Forum.  When I was on it before it had a different one.  Now that I'm hooked up again it will be fun following the action.  I will be putting my Series II Gt into the detail shop tomorrow to get it ready for the festivities.  I'd do it myself but I haven't got the time to do that and run the business.  Thanks to Stimpy and the crowd for all the help.<P>Big O<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000030||DXR_DAD||03-02-2000||01:13 AM||||Glad you made it Big O  Nice to talk to someone in my area and that I can stop by and see every now and then. I think I'll have my son DXR_WILL do the detail job on mine. I to have very little time but I will make time for the show. Looking foward to the event, hanging out with the rest of The Golden Gate Fieros members, and meeting your son (stimpy)<P>See ya!!<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000031||stimpy||03-02-2000||08:19 AM||||Hey Paw! Glad to see you made it.  Guess I will have to keep the language clean now. Sounds like we got us a bit of a shindig and a happenin! Sorry to hear that you are farming out my detailing duties. Check in wih you later. <BR>BTW- Some people want to know about an ACE conversion vs dealing with Chris West. ||||reg||1
Z||000032||Big O||03-02-2000||12:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>Hey Paw! Glad to see you made it.  Guess I will have to keep the language clean now. Sounds like we got us a bit of a shindig and a happenin! Sorry to hear that you are farming out my detailing duties. Check in wih you later. <BR>BTW- Some people want to know about an ACE conversion vs dealing with Chris West. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>For those who are considering farming out your Fiero to anyone for an engine swap, you need to be very careful who you choose, have lots of patience, and do a LOT of research before you open your wallet WIDE.  I would never slam anyone over the net as that's not politically correct.  I will say that I sent my vehicle to an "un-named" firm in the Rockies who claimed to be "experts" in this field.  I was less than satisfied with the results and would not recommend them to anyone.  On the other hand, Chris West is a perfectionist who understands quality and I would recommend him highly.  Just have a lot of patience because he will take all of the time necessary to do the job right.<P>Big O<P>||||reg||10
